          "text": "Clinical Indication:\nHistory of combined generalized and focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures beginning at age 28. Seizures occur approximately once per year and are drug responsive. Etiology is unknown. Current antiseizure medication is zonisamide.\n\nTechnique:\nRoutine digital scalp EEG was recorded using electrodes placed according to the International 10–20 system. The recording was reviewed using standard referential and bipolar montages.\n\nFindings:\nThe waking background is organized, symmetric, and reactive, without focal slowing. No focal or generalized epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures are identified.\n\nImpression:\nNormal routine awake EEG. No epileptiform abnormalities or electrographic seizures are seen. A normal routine EEG does not exclude epilepsy.",
